CloudBurrow patch 21 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1409). Applies after patch 0020; needs
googlesqlite patch 0032.

The gap: patch 0020's triggers round a value written to a top-level
parameterized NUMERIC(P, S) or BIGNUMERIC(P, S) column only. BigQuery
rounds a STRUCT's field, an ARRAY's element and a REPEATED RECORD's
field, at any depth, by the field's roundingMode, else the table's
defaultRoundingMode, else ROUND_HALF_AWAY_FROM_ZERO, and refuses one
past its precision OUT_OF_RANGE
(https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/schemas#rounding_mode).

The patch makes, for each top-level column that holds such a field (a
RECORD, or a REPEATED NUMERIC or RECORD), the same AFTER INSERT and
AFTER UPDATE OF triggers, calling googlesqlite_round_decimal_nested with
a spec of where the fields are, their precisions, scales and modes. So
every write path (DML, insertAll, loads, the Storage Write API, query
destinations) rounds them, as it rounds a top-level column.

